# Offline pin notes — gpw-hirshfeld-kpoints

## Method

Hirshfeld \(V/V_{\mathrm{free}}\) from the **multi-k** GPW PBE valence density
(k-summed \(\rho=\sum_k w_k\rho_k\); in-tree exponential free-atom model) →
MBD@rsSCS with scaled α/C6/R (same libMBD free-atom tables as `gpw-mbd-ice` /
`gpw-mbd-hirshfeld`).

## Why not stock CP2K QS?

CP2K 2026.1 `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` is only DFTD2|DFTD3|DFTD3(BJ)|DFTD4 — no
stock TS/MBD. Hard pin is the ATV product under fixed settings (CUTOFF 200 Ry,
Monkhorst–Pack 2×2×2, TR fold, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, GTH-PBE, water dimer 12 Å),
cross-checked vs free-atom MBD and the dual in-tree Hirshfeld kernel (same as
`gpw-mbd-hirshfeld`).

## Geometry

Same water dimer as `gpw-mbd-ice` / `gpw-mbd-hirshfeld` / `gpw-ts-ice`.

## Pin (product settings)

```
E_disp = -1.1479849553026611e-03 Ha
volumes (O H H O H H) ≈ 0.7403 0.6529 0.6529 0.7153 0.5784 0.5784
CUTOFF 200 Ry, k-mesh 2×2×2 TR, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, GTH-PBE, water dimer 12 Å
```
